WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.790
- [Mark] All right, Alex.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.250
Alex, where are you from originally?

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.663
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.663 --> 00:00:07.520
- [Alex] I grew up in
La Canada, California,

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.410
in between Pasadena and La Crescenta.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.340
A lot of people don't
know exactly where it is,

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.510
but it's a small kind of
bubble, very wealthy town.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.730
- [Mark] Yeah, basically
outside of Pasadena.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.040
And how'd you grow up?

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.233
With both your parents?

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:22.380
- Yes.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.800
Both my parents were...

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.883
Yes, they raised me.

00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:26.673
- [Mark] And how was your childhood?

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.380
- Some parts were good.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.320
Some parts were bad.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.800
My mom was a very violent alcoholic,

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.193
very condescending, violent.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.840
She was the type of person that

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.060
if I got a 95 on a test,

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:41.893
she'd be like,

00:00:41.893 --> 00:00:44.690
"Okay, well, you couldn't get 100?"

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.260
I just never felt good enough.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.850
So, that kind of messed
with my self-esteem.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.170
And when she got drunk
she was very violent

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.923
and she knew how to scrap.

00:00:57.079 --> 00:00:59.323
So it was kind of rough at some points.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:04.000
- [Mark] And then where'd your
life go when you left home?

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.010
- Well, actually, I got
kicked out when I was 19,

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.150
right after high school.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.260
I got held back in sixth grade.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.380
And two months out of high school,

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.350
my dad passed away,
- [Mark] Sorry.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.560
- And I moved back home.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.100
And then I went to Santa
Barbara City College

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.310
to try to get a degree

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.410
in about 2011,

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.243
I believe.

00:01:26.243 --> 00:01:28.090
He passed away 2010.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.350
So.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:33.520
- [Mark] And how'd you end up down here?

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.150
- [Alex] So basically,

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:39.160
I started using heroin in Santa Barbara.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.350
Of course it got dry.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.883
I knew somebody down
here that could get some.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:50.210
I went on vacation with
my mom to San Diego

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:55.040
and my friend drug dealer wasn't
picking up and I was sick.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.840
And so I didn't know what to do.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.740
And I just dro...

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.520
I literally took her car,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.430
drove three hours from San
Diego, unbeknownst to her,

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:04.930
to Skid Row,

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:07.087
driving around, asking people,

00:02:07.087 --> 00:02:09.883
"You know where I can
get this, that, this?"

00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:13.390
- [Mark] Did it take you longer
than two minutes to find it?

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.013
- [Alex] It literally, it
probably took about maybe,

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.573
yeah, 10 minutes.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.100
10 minutes of...

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.550
Yeah.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.550
And that's what started it.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.820
- [Mark] And then are
you staying down here?

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.140
- [Alex] No, I'm not staying down here.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.880
- [Mark] Here's not good enough?

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.330
- [Alex] Yeah, unfortunately.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:33.700
- [Mark] So where do you live now?

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.260
- [Alex] I live in Pasadena.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.093
- [Mark] Okay.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.940
And are you working at all?

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.390
- [Alex] I used to work at
P.F. Chang's for two years.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.430
And in order for me to get
sober, I decided to quit.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.940
But that didn't really work out,

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:48.773
but

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.540
I actually...

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.780
of course, drug addicts have a plan

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.170
but I have these medications
that will help me get on,

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.730
something called Suboxone

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.160
which you can wean yourself off of.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.450
And so that was the main
reason coming down here,

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.400
is to, try to help me get sober.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.320
So I'm looking at the next
week hopefully to get sober

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.610
and really like do this thing.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.530
I'm miserable.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:18.030
Yeah, it's a very soul sucking...

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.610
- [Mark] How long have you been using?

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.253
- Over the span of seven years,

00:03:22.675 --> 00:03:23.508
on and off.

00:03:23.508 --> 00:03:26.250
Longest I had sober was 16 months.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.360
- [Mark] And do your parents know you're

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.340
using heroin?

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.730
- My dad never knew before he died.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.330
He knew I smoked weed,

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.323
but yes, my mother does know,

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.273
unfortunately.

00:03:39.551 --> 00:03:41.507
- [Mark] And then what
are you doing for money?

00:03:41.507 --> 00:03:42.607
- What I do for money,

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:45.973
another long story,

00:03:45.973 --> 00:03:47.610
grandparents passed away.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:51.940
They had a trust fund for me,
since my dad wasn't alive.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.290
The trust went to natural born Bertus,

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.760
which is my last name.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.210
So my mom didn't get it.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.803
So my brother and I,

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:04.920
every year we get 5% of
the money from this trust.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.980
And at first, when I
was sober, it was great.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:08.840
I was doing good.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.310
And then the second I relapsed,

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.430
my habit was out of control.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:16.230
And yeah, it's a blessing in disguise.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.620
So I'm hoping this next year,

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.680
that's why I'm trying
to get clean right now

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:23.650
is so like I don't start the
next year with all this money

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.483
and just

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.834
blow it all and waste on my life.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:29.667
Man, I love my life.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:32.213
I hate the way I'm living right now.

00:04:34.217 --> 00:04:35.630
- [Mark] And do you have any

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:38.580
relationships with anybody?

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:40.920
I mean, do you have friends?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.240
Do you have a girlfriend,
anything like that?

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.124
- I actually...

00:04:45.124 --> 00:04:46.140
Yeah, I did have an ex-girl...

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.683
Or I did have a girlfriend,

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:51.540
she cheat on me, I kicked her out.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:55.440
Actually my best friend just
passed away on the 23rd.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.026
His funeral was yesterday.

00:04:58.026 --> 00:04:58.859
- [Mark] (mumbles) sorry.

00:04:58.859 --> 00:05:00.160
- And

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.500
yeah, so it's...

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.480
And then I found out this morning that

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.210
my brother is an early alcoholic,

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.800
my dad passed away in his arms.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.210
And

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:11.820
they said that his liver is so bad

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:15.983
that he has a 50/50 chance
of dying in the next 90 days.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:20.710
So, we're all just praying for him and

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.850
it's also surreal.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:24.280
It's all like, "Holy shit, man."

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.730
And that's another reason
why I want to shape up.

00:05:28.504 --> 00:05:29.990
- [Mark] How did your friend pass away?

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.590
- They found him next to a
meth pipe, which is strange

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:35.733
'cause usually people don't
pass away from a meth pipe.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.390
So my home girl thinks it
was laced with fentanyl

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:42.053
or something,

00:05:42.053 --> 00:05:42.890
but we don't know.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:45.296
And I'm not about to ask his family.

00:05:45.296 --> 00:05:46.830
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:47.663
Wow.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.705
Well, good luck with everything, man.

00:05:50.705 --> 00:05:52.240
Thank you so much for talking to me.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.740
- [Alex] I grew up from a
relatively wealthy family.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:59.623
I had opportunities like
no other, and I still do.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.412
- [Mark] That doesn't mean
you're immune to (mumbles).

00:06:03.412 --> 00:06:05.090
- [Alex] (mumbles) addict.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:05.923
- [Mark] Happens to everybody.

00:06:05.923 --> 00:06:06.756
- [Alex] Exactly.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.093
- [Mark] Okay, thank you.

00:06:09.093 --> 00:06:10.880
- Yeah, absolutely, man.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:11.863
Thank you so much.

